Anaheim, California lemon law (the Song Beverly Consumer Warranty Act) holds manufacturers accountable for poorly produced, problematic cars. At CLINE APC, our consumer law attorneys help Anaheim clients understand our state’s lemon law and learn how to obtain justice.

These factors indicate manufacturer mistakes entitle you to a refund or replacement vehicle under lemon law in Anaheim, California:

- The vehicle manufacturer has made at least two or more attempts to repair a warranty-covered defect, or

- The vehicle has been out of service for more than 30 days while being repaired for warranty-covered problems; and

- The vehicle has several warranty-covered problems, which were not caused by the consumer’s abuse or neglect of the vehicle.

It’s important to note that there is a time limit for seeking compensation under Anaheim, California lemon law - even with the aid of a lemon lawyer in Anaheim. Your lemon car’s defect must first occur within the defined terms of the manufacturer or dealer warranty.

Despite a common misunderstanding, your vehicle’s problem does not need to occur within the first 18 months after purchase or before the odometer reaches 18,000 miles. The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty.

